  "summary": "One world, two Runs, and the only thing that differs between them is the objective each one stated. The warm Rental holds the whole image and a checked copy of the 40GB dataset and is a second from ready at 4 USD an hour. The cold one holds neither and is nearly sixteen minutes from ready at 2 USD an hour. A Run that asked for the cheapest capacity gets the cold machine, because that is what cheapest means. A Run that asked for the fastest start gets the warm one and pays double for it, because that is what fastest_start means, and the decision records EARLIEST_START rather than claiming it compared prices. Until the objective ordered candidates it was a word the public API accepted and nothing read: every Run was ranked on one dollar score whose time term was a weight nothing populates, so a Run that asked to start soonest was placed on whichever machine was a cent cheaper and, when prices tied, on whichever offer ID sorted first.",
